& [Question]
  + can Slice2 drive exact compact READY chains without a provider while preserving the meaning of Slice1 records

& [Finding]
  + CompactSessionCommand Advance already accepts exact registry digest session sequence record digest and quota and returns an owned successor registry plus compact response
  + the quota-eight governed fixture demonstrably yields READY then terminal across two calls
  + Slice1 IterationRecord intentionally binds model request sanitized response and call identity
  + a provider-free stepper cannot populate IterationRecord without fabricating provider evidence

& [Delineation]
  + deterministic procedure advancement and provider-attributed iteration are different records
  + Slice2 must not emit dummy request response model or call fields
  + Slice3 may later join one admitted provider call with one proven deterministic advancement into IterationRecord

& [SelectedPureSurface]
  + DeterministicAdvanceRecord carries zero-based index predecessor handle exact compact response and exclusive ready or terminal successor
  + DeterministicDriveResult carries policy opening identity ordered advance records successor registry and either exact terminal observation or stopped head reason and reentry availability
  + drive_bound_session accepts one validated bound session and RunPolicy and applies at most maximum_tool_calls sequential exact ADVANCE commands
  + terminal path performs exact READ and stopped cap path returns the current READY head without another mutation
  + compact refusal or invariant fault returns a faulted stopped result at the last validated head with no invented successor

& [RequiredProof]
  + quota sixty-four reaches the byte-identical P0 terminal result in one advance
  + quota eight yields exactly one READY projection then terminal outcome
  + quota one with cap two stops at an exact live reentry head and resumes to byte-identical terminal outcome when explicitly driven again
  + stale opening handle changed successor digest terminal-as-ready and response fault refuse
  + normalized drive result replay is deterministic across repeated fixture runs

& [ActivationPrerequisites]
  + preserve a Slice2 implementation source naming this distinct record boundary
  + bind current canonical Slice1 proof and exact compact-session implementation identities
  + issue effectless Slice2 authority only after completed-work review
  + retain provider request construction and IterationRecord assembly for Slice3

